Data license of the GeoDevelopment Observatory of Bolivia (GDO-Bolivia)

The code in this repository (src/, scripts/, tests/, notebooks/, site/) is released
under the MIT License (see LICENSE). This file covers the data.

The observatory's data files are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/:

  - data/            one folder per dataset: the published panels (CSV and Parquet), the
                     same data wide (GeoPackage and GeoJSON; their boundaries follow the
                     exception below), the metadata (datapackage.json, Frictionless) and
                     the generated documentation (README.md)
  - the variable catalog named in project.yaml (definitions_gdo-bolivia.csv)
  - geo/units.*      the unit list (geo IDs, names, codes, areas)
  - geo/crosswalks/  the crosswalks between scales

You may share and adapt them for any purpose, including commercially, provided you give
appropriate credit to the GeoDevelopment Observatory of Bolivia and to the original
sources, provide a link to the license, and indicate if changes were made.

Exceptions

  - Boundaries. geo/boundaries/, site/data/*.geojson and raw/boundaries/sdsn2025/ come from
    SDSN Bolivia's municipal map of 2025 (Límites Municipales Bolivia 2025: the 343
    municipalities and indigenous autonomies, from the Ministerio de Planificación del
    Desarrollo, the Instituto Nacional de Estadística and the Viceministerio de Autonomías).
    SDSN Bolivia licenses it under CC BY 4.0, and its citation is mandatory: "SDSN Bolivia
    (2025). Límites Municipales Bolivia 2025 [Archivo shapefile].
    https://sdsnbolivia.org/datos-espaciales/". raw/protected_areas/sdsn2025/ (Áreas
    protegidas Bolivia 2025, SDSN Bolivia) states no open license and is kept with SDSN
    Bolivia's permission, with the same citation requirement. The geo IDs follow GADM
    4.1's numbering, and geo/units keeps GADM's codes and names (gid, name_gadm) as source
    keys; no GADM geometry is distributed (version 0.1 of the observatory did). Versions 0.2
    and 0.3 used geoBoundaries' public-domain polygons from GeoBolivia.
  - Original sources. Each dataset is derived from third-party data whose own terms and
    required credits are listed in its metadata (data/<dataset>/datapackage.json,
    "sources"), its README and its page of the website. Where a source requires otherwise,
    its terms prevail. The Atlas de los ODS en Bolivia 2026 (datasets sdg and sdg01 ...
    sdg17; © Universidad Privada Boliviana) is licensed by SDSN Bolivia under CC BY 4.0,
    and its authors ask to be cited: Andersen, L.E. & Argandoña,
    F. (2026). Atlas de los ODS en Bolivia 2026: Brechas y tendencias del desarrollo
    sostenible en las Entidades Territoriales Autónomas, 2012–2024. La Paz: Universidad
    Privada Boliviana, SDSN Bolivia.
  - raw/ holds the original inputs as received; they keep their sources' terms.
  - Citation. Cite each dataset's original sources first, then the observatory, which
    processes and maintains the data ("Mendez, C. (2026). GeoDevelopment Observatory of
    Bolivia. https://quarcs-lab.github.io/gdo4bolivia/"), then its other sources: the list
    is in the dataset's README and page, and geo.cite("<dataset>") prints it.
  - Website images (images/, media/) keep the terms stated in the website's credits.
